<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    WJSS shared motion composition (ACCELERATED-CLEANING-INTEGRATION-01, Owner decision:
    option A, the approved minimal shared motion-composition library).

    WHY THIS PROJECT EXISTS
    The physical-capable Manual Motion port must be constructed in two hosts: the isolated
    Owner-local commissioning application and the TEST_HARDWARE_DRY cleaning composition. It
    cannot live in either host, because a host is not referenceable as a library; it cannot live
    in the motion-library adapter, because that adapter's documented boundary forbids an
    Application reference; and it cannot live in the Application, because the Application may
    not reference an adapter (that would be a cycle).

    This assembly is the smallest thing that resolves the triangle. It references the adapter
    (for the internal controller owner) and the Application (for the typed port and session), and
    it OWNS the two shared source files:

      MotionLibraryManualMotionPort.cs   the hardware-capable port (enum mapping only)
      ManualMotionProfileFile.cs         the Owner-local profile reader

    The isolated commissioning application LINKS those two files from here rather than keeping
    a second copy. There is still exactly ONE port implementation and ONE profile reader, and the
    application keeps its own two project references and stays unreferenced by anything.

    WHAT THIS PROJECT DOES NOT DO
    It adds no motion adapter, no native entry point, no command vocabulary, no text channel,
    no raw command, no discovery surface and no new safety authority. It composes the existing
    controller owner, the existing closed commissioning plan, the existing typed Stop session
    and the existing Application session. Nothing here opens a handle, loads a native module or
    touches a controller at construction time: the owner proves its gate at Open.

    SOURCE-AUTHORED IN ARENA. NOT COMPILED IN ARENA (no .NET SDK in the Arena sandbox). The
    Owner-local Windows build and test run are the validation of record.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Wjss.MotionComposition</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Wjss.MotionComposition</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../../adapters/motion-library/Wjss.Adapters.MotionLibrary.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../../packages/application/Wjss.Runtime.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../../packages/contracts/Wjss.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../../packages/domain/Wjss.Domain.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../../packages/time/Wjss.Time.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
